{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":69777936,"ns":0,"title":"Gunslinger effect","extract":"The gunslinger effect, also sometimes called Bohr's law or the gunfighter's dilemma, is a psychophysical theory which says that an intentional or willed movement is slower than an automatic or reaction movement. The concept is named after physicist Niels Bohr, who first deduced that the person who draws second in a gunfight will actually win the shoot-out.","description":"Psychophysical theory","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}